><a href="/rails">Where the money settles</a><a href="/bounties">The Bounty Board</a><a href="/field-study">The Field Study</a><a href="/credit">Regulars&#39; credit</a><a href="/rights">What&#39;s yours</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/deprecation">API versioning and deprecation policy</a><a href="/wind-down">If the lights go off</a><a href="/becoming">What this is trying to prove</a></nav>
    </header>
    <section>
        <p class="menu-meta">Unsigned host-history summary. The timeline, tier and gap counts are derived context, not a signed artifact. Each timeline entry links a corpus original: retain it and an independently established issuer key, verify its signature, then inspect snapshot.round.hosts for rows whose url exactly matches the requested endpoint, including the query string. Top-level snapshot metadata alone cannot establish absence of endpoint observations. The existing scvd-evidence verify-source command with --subject selects verified exact-URL rows; read their observation dates separately from snapshot publication time. A missing observed_at means the observation date of the signed row is unknown, not the snapshot publication time or a date supplied by this unsigned timeline; it cannot establish observation-age freshness. To authenticate several weeks, retain and verify each cited original and report its own row dates and gaps. One verified snapshot does not authenticate other weeks or this summary.</p>
        <p class="menu-desc"><strong>indeterminate — 1 of 4, W35–W38</strong> — fewer rounds than the rule needs, or our coverage of this host was suspect in the window. The rule and every tier are at <a href="/criteria">/criteria</a>; the rows are below. Never a ranking, and never a verdict without its derivation and denominator beside it.</p>
        <p class="menu-meta">Latest observation: <code>ready</code> on 2026-09-15T16:30:35.575Z. Rounds since first sighting: 6; probed: 1; missed: 5 (our coverage of this host: 16.7%). Our own coverage was suspect somewhere in the window, which the tier already reflects.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Every round, including the ones we missed</h2>
        <section class="probe-strip" data-host="weather.parklandarchives.com">
    <div class="ticks" role="img" aria-label="7 rounds 2026-W32 to 2026-W38, 1 probed"><a class="tick" data-outcome="gap" data-week="2026-W32" href="https://scvd.store/corpus/1.json" title="2026-W32: not walked — before_first_sighting" aria-label="2026-W32: not walked — before_first_sighting"></a><a class="tick" data-outcome="gap" data-week="2026-W33" href="https://scvd.store/corpus/2.json" title="2026-W33: not walked — listed_not_walked" aria-label="2026-W33: not walked — listed_not_walked"></a><a class="tick" data-outcome="gap" data-week="2026-W34" href="https://scvd.store/corpus/3.json" title="2026-W34: not walked — listed_not_walked" aria-label="2026-W34: not walked — listed_not_walked"></a><a class="tick" data-outcome="gap" data-week="2026-W35" href="https://scvd.store/corpus/4.json" title="2026-W35: not walked — listed_not_walked" aria-label="2026-W35: not walked — listed_not_walked"></a><a class="tick" data-outcome="gap" data-week="2026-W36" href="https://scvd.store/corpus/5.json" title="2026-W36: not walked — listed_not_walked" aria-label="2026-W36: not walked — listed_not_walked"></a><a class="tick" data-outcome="gap" data-week="2026-W37" href="https://scvd.store/corpus/7.json" title="2026-W37: not walked — listed_not_walked" aria-label="2026-W37: not walked — listed_not_walked"></a><a class="tick" data-outcome="ready" data-week="2026-W38" href="https://scvd.store/corpus/8.json" title="2026-W38: ready" aria-label="2026-W38: ready"></a></div>
    <p class="menu-meta">Every round on the chain, 2026-W32 → 2026-W38: 1 probed of 7.
    <span class="key"><span class="tick" data-outcome="ready"></span> ready</span>
    <span class="key"><span class="tick" data-outcome="not_ready"></span> not ready</span>
    <span class="key"><span class="tick" data-outcome="unreachable"></span> unreachable</span>
    <span class="key"><span class="tick" data-outcome="gap"></span> not walked — the reason is on the tick</span>.
    A gap is a fact about our cadence, not about the door.</p>
  </section>
